# Keep the deployment bundle to the application only.
# Same syntax as .gitignore. Applies to CLI and Git deployments alike.

.planning/
docs/
tests/
drizzle/
*.md
.github/

# The test-harness configs go with the directory they configure. `playwright.config.ts`
# imports `./tests/e2e/_required-env` at the top level, so with `tests/` excluded and the
# config shipped, `next build` compiled fine and then FAILED type checking on Vercel with
# TS2307 — a build error that cannot reproduce locally, because locally `tests/` exists.
# The two vitest configs reference `tests/` only through string globs and so did not
# break, but they are harness for an excluded directory just the same and closing the
# class costs nothing. None of the three is imported by anything under `src/`.
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
vitest.db.config.ts

# drizzle/ is excluded deliberately, not incidentally: migrations are applied from a
# developer machine by `pnpm db:migrate:prod` against the session pooler, never at build
# time and never at runtime. Shipping the migration files would put a build-time or
# preview-deploy migration one line of config away from running against production.
